additions.what:
Add a <VisualRecap> with title="Build from the root up". rule="new runs the base-class constructor first (so the root runs first), then this class's property initializers, then the rest of this class's body; a property is undefined until its initializer runs (§8.7, §8.17)." code={`class bus_item extends base_item;
  bit [31:0] addr = 32'h100;   // runs after base_item::new returns
  function new(string name = "bus_item");
    super.new(name);           // first executable statement
  endfunction
endclass`}. mistake="Leaving out super.new(name): the compiler inserts super.new() with no arguments, which fails to compile if the base needs an argument and silently passes the base's defaults if it has them (§8.15)." inTestbench="A static counter plus a const id set in new gives every transaction a unique, fixed id. UVM objects declare new(string name = "..."), components declare new(string name, uvm_component parent), and components build their children in build_phase, not in new." children: the compact Quick Take floors SVG with three bug markers: on a super.new arrow, 'missing: base gets its defaults'; on a body cell, 'addr = addr; leaves the property at its default'; on the base body cell, 'virtual call: the child's override reads undefined fields'. No animation.

Add an 'Anatomy of one randomize() call on frame' ArchitectureDiagram (cellWidth={120} gapX={48}, spreadAnchors).

- **Container** 'object f (class frame)' with three generic nodes:
  - 'random variables' (sublabel 'kind, len, payload[]');
  - 'named blocks' (sublabel 'c_len c_payload c_long c_buffer', badge 'constraint_mode');
  - 'state variables' (sublabel 'none here; rand_mode(0) makes one', state dim).
- **Outside the container:**
  - the call 'f.randomize() with {…}' (sublabel 'inline: kind == LONG');
  - 'solver' (sublabel 'all active hard rules at once, §18.3');
  - two outcomes: ok 'one legal combination: returns 1' and error 'none: returns 0, old values kept (§18.6.3)'.
- **Edges:**
  - control from the call to the solver, labelled 'inline';
  - data from the members to the solver, labelled 'active';
  - causal from the solver to the outcomes, labelled 'found' and 'none'.

Keep edge labels to 10 characters or fewer and prefer vertical edges (the default gapY is 76). The caption maps each box to its glossary term and says this is the frame class from Make It Work. Run DIAGRAM_KIT_REPORT=1 npx vitest run tests/lib/diagram-kit-content.test.ts, because any new layout warning fails CI.
